      "id": "2122723269132603790",
      "text": "Wow!😲 #SouthKorea, the nation that recently reversed its plan to phase out all its #Nuclear reactors, now needs 6,000 metric tons (13.2 Million lbs) of #Uranium fuel as drummed #U3O8 ⚛️🛢️☢️ that it wants delivered over 10 years from 2028 to 2037 at 600 tons (1.32M lbs) per year.🇰🇷🚛 It's Nuclear utility KHNP has issued a public Invitation to Tender wanting interested suppliers to submit offers by 28 December.🧾📨\n\nThe most remarkable aspect of this ITT is the removal of prescribed price floors and ceilings from the Spot price related component of their pricing formula.  In the past they have set strict pricing limits which have led to \"no bids\" received.  This time their pricing formula allows the bidding supplier to offer a Base Escalated Fixed Price for at least 30% of their proposed contract plus Spot Market Referenced for the remaining portion of up to 70%, with NO FLOOR PRICES and NO PRESCRIBED CEILING PRICE LIMITS on the Spot referenced portion.🤯\n\nTalk about reversals!↪️  A few years ago South Korea had planned to halt all further Uranium purchasing and now they are in the market seeking 13.2 Million lbs of new supply AND have reversed their prior policy of setting strict price limits for fixed price contracts.  A sign of the times!⚛️⤴️⛽️ + ⤵️⛏️🗜️🤠🐂\nhttps://www.khnp.co.kr/eng/selectBbsNttView.do?key=566&bbsNo=213&nttNo=77754",
